# Introduction

A DP-PBEsol model for CdTe. [1,2]

Here, an accurate machine-learning force field (ML-FF), named the CdTe-PBEsol-model, is developed for CdTe systems based on extensive quantum mechanics (QM) simulations. We apply this ML-FF to investigate the structural phase transitions and the behavior of dislocation decomposition and movement in CdTe during deformation. Additionally, we examine Homoepitaxial Film Growth. Our simulation results elucidate the atomic mechanisms underlying experimental phenomena in CdTe materials, thereby demonstrating the accuracy of the developed ML-FF.

# Training

the main training datasets are generated using a concurrent learning algorithm, as implemented in the Deep Potential GENerator (DP-GEN) [3]. The DeePMD-kit package is used for training [4]. The sizes of the embedding and fitting nets are set to (25, 50, 100) and (120, 120, 120), respectively. The cut-off radius is set to 6 Å and the smoothing starts from 5.0 Å. The Adam stochastic gradient descent method with the default hyperparameter settings provided by the TensorFlow packag was used to train the DP models.The learning rate varies from 0.001 to 3.51 × 10<sup>–8</sup> with an exponential decay in the total of 1 × 10<sup>6</sup> training steps. The model compression scheme was applied in this work for boosting the computational efficiency of the MD simulation [5].
More details can be found in [1].

# Use model

1. Download and install LAMMPS: https://docs.lammps.org/Manual.html
2. Download and install DeePMD-kit: https://github.com/deepmodeling/deepmd-kit
3. Prepare input data for LAMMPS
4. Download the model. note: "type_map": ["Cd","Te"]
5. Run MD with LAMMPS: https://github.com/deepmodeling/deepmd-kit/blob/master/doc/third-party/lammps.md
   for example:
   read_data	./CdTe.data
   mass            1 112.414 # Cd
   mass            2 127.60 #Te
   pair_style	deepmd ./CdTe-PBEsol.pb
   pair_coeff      * *

